"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Pirates\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Group\",\n      \"description\": \"Pirates are seafaring outlaws who have operated across different time periods, regions, and cultures, often challenging the established order and living by their own rules. They are known for their swift attacks, division of spoils, and a strict code of conduct, and have left a lasting legacy in popular culture and folklore.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Time Period\": \"From ancient times to the early 18th century, with the Golden Age of Piracy spanning from the late 17th century to the early 18th century\",\n        \"Regions\": \"Mediterranean, Caribbean, and North Africa\",\n        \"Cultural Impact\": \"Captured the imagination of people around the world, featured in folklore, books, movies, and television shows\",\n        \"Behavior\": \"Flamboyant personalities, cunning tactics, ruthless behavior, and swift attacks on merchant ships and coastal communities\",\n        \"Motivation\": \"Lure of gold, silver, and other valuable goods\",\n        \"Code of Conduct\": \"Operated under a strict code known as the Pirate Code, governing division of spoils and resolution of disputes\",\n        \"Public Perception\": \"Often seen as heroes by the common people, viewed as symbols of freedom and defiance against colonialism and imperialism\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"coastal towns\",\n      \"type\": \"Location\",\n      \"description\": \"Coastal towns are settlements located near the sea, often targeted by pirates for raids and attacks.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Type\": \"Settlement\",\n        \"Location\": \"Near the sea\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"governments\",\n      \"type\": \"Organization\",\n      \"description\": \"Governments are formal institutions that manage the affairs of a state or region, often involved in the creation and enforcement of laws and policies.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Role in Piracy\": \"Sponsorship and Regulation\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Pirate Code\",\n      \"type\": \"Code of Conduct\",\n      \"description\": \"The Pirate Code was a set of rules and regulations used by pirate crews to govern various aspects of their operations, including the division of spoils and the resolution of disputes among crew members.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"To govern the operations of pirate crews, including the division of spoils and the resolution of disputes.\",\n        \"Nature\": \"Strict\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"The Pirate Code\",\n      \"type\": \"Code of Conduct\",\n      \"description\": \"The Pirate Code was a set of rules used by pirates to maintain order and discipline aboard their ships, ensuring fair treatment and decision-making among crew members.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"Maintain order and discipline aboard pirate ships\",\n        \"Scope\": \"Ensuring fair treatment and decision-making among crew members\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"common people\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Group\",\n      \"description\": \"The common people, also known as the general populace, are the ordinary citizens of a society, often contrasted with the elite or ruling classes.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Perception of Pirates\": \"Often viewed pirates as heroes and rebels\",\n        \"Economic Status\": \"Ordinary citizens, typically not part of the elite or ruling classes\",\n        \"Historical Context\": \"Lived during the period of the Golden Age of Piracy, a time marked by widespread piracy and colonial expansion\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"France\",\n      \"type\": \"Country\",\n      \"description\": \"France is a country in Western Europe known for its rich history, cultural heritage, and significant role in global affairs.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Geographical Locati