l patrols contributed to the decline of piracy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Affected By\",\n      \"Anti-Piracy Laws\",\n      \"Anti-piracy laws were implemented to reduce pirate activities and punish offenders.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Affected By\",\n      \"Harsh Punishments\",\n      \"Harsh punishments for piracy offenses helped curb the prevalence of piracy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Featured In\",\n      \"Popular Culture and Folklore\",\n      \"Pirates have been immortalized in popular culture and folklore, often depicted in tales of adventure and daring.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Featured In\",\n      \"Books, Movies, and Television Shows\",\n      \"Pirates have been a popular subject in books, movies, and television shows, contributing to their enduring legacy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Included Notable Figures\",\n      \"Blackbeard, Captain Kidd, and Calico Jack\",\n      \"These legendary pirates were among the most feared and well-known during the Golden Age of Piracy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"coastal towns\",\n      \"Targeted By\",\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Coastal towns were frequently targeted by pirates for raids and attacks, especially during the era of the Barbary pirates.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"coastal towns\",\n      \"Located In\",\n      \"Europe\",\n      \"Some coastal towns that were targeted by pirates were located in Europe, particularly those along the Mediterranean and Atlantic coasts.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"governments\",\n      \"Sponsored\",\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"Some governments sponsored pirates, viewing piracy as a means to generate income and weaken their enemies.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"governments\",\n      \"Enforced\",\n      \"Anti-Piracy Laws\",\n      \"Governments enforced anti-piracy laws to curb pirate activities and maintain maritime security.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"governments\",\n      \"Conducted\",\n      \"Naval Patrols\",\n      \"Governments conducted naval patrols to combat piracy and protect their shipping interests.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"governments\",\n      \"Imposed\",\n      \"Harsh Punishments\",\n      \"Governments imposed harsh punishments for piracy offenses to deter potential pirates and maintain law and order.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"governments\",\n      \"Cracked Down On\",\n      \"Pirate Activity\",\n      \"European governments, such as Britain and France, cracked down on pirate activity in the Caribbean and other regions, contributing to the decline of piracy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirate Code\",\n      \"Governed By\",\n      \"Pirate Crews\",\n      \"Pirate crews operated under the Pirate Code, which provided a framework for their conduct and operations.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirate Code\",\n      \"Regulated\",\n      \"Division of Spoils\",\n      \"The Pirate Code regulated how spoils were divided among the crew members, ensuring a fair and orderly distribution.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Pirate Code\",\n      \"Regulated\",\n      \"Resolution of Disputes\",\n      \"The Pirate Code provided guidelines for resolving disputes among crew members, maintaining order and cohesion within the pirate community.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"The Pirate Code\",\n      \"Used By\",\n      \"Pirates\",\n      \"The Pirate Code was used by pirates to govern their behavior and interactions on board their ships.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"The Pirate Code\",\n      \"Ensured\",\n      \"Fair Treatment\",\n      \"The Pirate Code ensured that all crew members were treated fairly and had a say in important decisions.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"The Pirate Code\",\n      \"Ensured\",\n      \"Order and Discipline\",\n      \"The Pirate Code helped maintain order and discipline among the pirate crew to ensure the ship\\\"s effective operation.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"common people\",\n      \"Viewed\",\n      \"pirates\",\n      \"The common people often saw pirates as heroes and rebels fighting against the oppressive forces of colonialism and imperialism.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"common people\",\n      \"Lived Under\",\n      \"colonialism and imperialism\",\n      \"The common people lived under the systems of colonialism and imperialism, which they often perceived as oppressive.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"France\",\n      \"Cracked Down On\",\n      \"Pirate Activity\",\n      \"France, along with Britain, played a crucial role in the decline of piracy by cracking down on pirate activities in the Caribbean and other regions during the early 18th century.\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}"